<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105271" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρισσ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, όν;</span>
		
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριττός</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Pl.
			<u>Lg.</u>
			782d
		</span></i>, etc.; 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριξός</span></b>  (q. v.): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίς</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>threefold,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				191
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				285.3
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρισσὸν ζεῦγος
			τρισσῶν</span> (sed leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριῶν</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> θεῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					924
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρᾶσις τ. γραφεῖσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					1208.24
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>:—Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Pr.</u>
				22.20
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				12.123
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in pl., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρεῖς</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				8.80
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				164
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>OC</u>
				479
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				645
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				504a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίτος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(2).129.8
			</span></i> (Mytil.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρισσοί,</span>
			=
			<i>shields,</i> misrendering of Hebr.
				<i>šelātî</i> through confusion
			with <i>šālōš</i>
			'three', <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>4 Ki.</u>
				11.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b> literal
			rendering of Hebr.
				<i>šālīš</i>
			'measure containing third part (of unknown unit)', <i><span class="en">
				Aq.
				<u>Is.</u>
				40.12
			</span></i>.</div>
